# AutoDeployer: rules for the builder

Read `docs/PLAN-v4.md` and `docs/WORKFLOW.md` before starting any issue. The plan's section C (Decisions log) is locked: do not change those decisions inside a feature PR. If you think one is wrong, open an issue and explain.

## Working agreement
- One issue per branch (`<issue-number>-<slug>`), one PR per issue, using the PR template. Build only what the acceptance criteria say; extra ideas become new issues.
- Work on the lowest-numbered `status:ready` issue in the current milestone.
- Do not start the runner (Phase 1c) before the Phase 0 spike report is approved.

## Architecture rules
- The core is a headless Go CLI (`cmd/autodeployer`, packages under `internal/`). The CLI is the product. The GUI is a separate repo and never spawns scripts itself.
- Every run is its own OS process. Closing a GUI must never kill a run.
- Layout: `project/` is replaced on promote; `data/` is machine-local and is never replaced, committed or deleted by promote.
- Real secrets live only in `data/env/<job-id>/.env.<profile>`. Only `*.example` templates are committed. Never commit `.env` files, logs or `data/` contents.
- Exit codes in `internal/exitcode` are a public contract. Do not renumber. JSON shapes and CLI flags change only together with `docs/design/CONTRACT.md`.
- Time: local machine time with offset in logs and file names; UTC stored in SQLite; order history by UTC.
- Encoding: decode child output per step code page on line boundaries; always write UTF-8 logs; never crash on undecodable bytes. `auto` means the machine default code page, no sniffing.
- Tree-kill only on timeout or cancel, never on normal completion. `detach: true` children must survive normal CLI exit.
- Mask secrets in logs and plan output. Never print secret values in confirmation summaries.

## Code rules
- Go 1.22+, standard library first, no CGO unless an issue allows it (single static Windows binary is a goal; prefer a pure-Go SQLite driver).
- Windows-only code goes behind build tags with a Unix equivalent where one makes sense.
- Error messages must be readable by non-developers (for example: `job.yaml: steps[1].command: file not found: run_java.bat`).
- Every PR runs `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` clean.
